## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design an online, scalable PCA solution with drift detection and actionable alerts, not just theoretical knowledge. It combines streaming preprocessing, incremental factor analysis, and interpretable thresholds with real-time latency goals suitable for fintech dashboards.

## Key Concepts

- IncrementalPCA vs batch PCA
- Online imputation and scaling
- Drift detection via explained variance and loadings
- Latency budgeting in streaming analytics
- Interpretability via region-aware loadings

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: online PCA scaffold
class OnlinePCAProcessor {
  constructor(nComponents = 10) {
    this.pca = new IncrementalPCA(n_components: nComponents)
    this.scaler = new StandardScaler()
    this.driftThreshold = 0.15
  }

  processBatch(batch) {
    // Impute missing values with column means
    const imputed = this.imputeMissing(batch)
    const scaled = this.scaler.fitTransform(imputed)
    const components = this.pca.partialFit(scaled)
    return this.detectDrift(components)
  }
}

